# Local junk
tmp/
uploads/
rag_data/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.venv/
.env
# User data directories at the repo ROOT only (not source code under src/).
# The previous `data/` matched src/finetune_studio/data/ and silently ignored
# any new source files added under that path — which broke the file-library
# build on fan-dragon. Use anchored patterns + explicit names instead.
# Everything under data/ is runtime state EXCEPT the one shipped seed file the
# app reads at startup (the default benchmark suite). This must be `/data/*`
# and not `/data/`: git does not descend into a directory excluded by a bare
# `/data/`, so the negations below could never re-include anything. An earlier
# unanchored `data/` also matched src/finetune_studio/data/ and silently
# ignored new source files — which broke the file-library build on fan-dragon.
/data/*
# Three-step re-include, and it must stay three steps: `/data/*` excludes the
# benchmarks DIR, and git never descends into an excluded dir, so the dir must
# be un-ignored before the file inside it can be. Then re-ignore everything
# else in benchmarks/ — a single `!/data/benchmarks/` exposed the runtime
# hf_cache/ tree (21 files) that had been invisible under the old bare /data/.
!/data/benchmarks/
/data/benchmarks/*
!/data/benchmarks/default.json
/.finetune-studio.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/projects/
/output/
/screenshots/
# Runtime dirs that were previously NOT ignored even though AGENTS.md lists
# them as "runtime artifacts, never committed": a user's corpus, downloaded
# weights, and inbound media staging all sat untracked-but-visible, one
# `git add -A` away from being committed.
/datasets/
/models/
/media/
# Build artifacts that should never enter version control. The llama.cpp
# build lives under .llama.cpp/ at the repo root (project-local, see
# LLAMA_CPP_DIR in install.sh) so the install scripts don't reach into
# $HOME for binaries.
/.llama.cpp/
/build/
/dist/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
# Common runtime / build artifacts
*.log
*.tmp
# Tool caches / local agent state — never repo content.
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
/.serena/
node_modules/
# Written into the repo root by unsloth at import time (compiled trainer
# copies + lock files). tests/test_import_smoke.py triggers it, so a plain
# `make test` would otherwise leave ~31 untracked files behind.
/unsloth_compiled_cache/

# Workspace-level OpenClaw files (Amy persona, handoff notes).
# These belong in ~/.openclaw/workspace/, NEVER inside a project repo.
IDENTITY.md
SOUL.md
USER.md
HANDOFF-*.md

# Local agent playbook + working notes (workflow guides, techniques, scratch).
# Deliberately NOT versioned — per Genor's request, 2026-09-11.
.agent/

# Session daily-notes logs (memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md) — local continuity, not project code.
/memory/
.openclaw/
